ot see -- from the defective one: bytes that are constants compiled into the application or derived from constants. Where the bytes come from decides it.', 'expected': 'a key produced by one of the generators the rule names', 'source_location': 'KeystoreSecretVault.kt:69', 'codes': 'CIPHER-NOBS-00 [not-observed] (2)', 'tools': 'ape:sata, monkey:fast', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 2 run(s) of the app; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator.', 'runtime_coverage_file': '/mnt/c/Users/Antonow/Documents/tcc_v3/outputs/rvsec_io_github_thatsfguy_meshcore_native_20261105/findings_all.coverage.json'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'CONTRIBUTING.md', 'content': '# Contributing\n\nShort version: **this is a personal, security-first app, and it is closed to feature requests.** It\'s released in the open so anyone can use it, audit it, or fork it — not as an open-ended community project soliciting features.\n\n## What\'s welcome\n\n- **Security reports.** This is the one kind of contribution I actively want. Report privately — see **[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md)**. Do not open a public issue or PR for a vulnerability.\n- **Bug reports for existing features.** If something that already ships is broken, a focused, reproducible bug report is welcome. Use the Bug report issue form.\n- **Forks.** The app is [AGPL-3.0](LICENSE). If you want it to do something it doesn\'t do, fork it and build that. That is the intended path for new functionality, and the licence exists precisely to let you.\n\n## What\'s not accepted\n\n- **Feature requests / "please add X" issues.** They\'ll be closed. Not a judgement on the idea — adding surface works directly against the security goal of this app (smallest, most static attack vector). Fork instead.\n- **Feature PRs.** Unsolicited PRs that add capabilities, dependencies, transports, or new protocols will be closed unmerged. This includes "quality of life" additions.\n- **Dependency / CI / build-pipeline changes from outside.** These are the highest-risk supply-chain surface and are not accepted from contributors. (Dependabot-style auto-bumping is intentionally off.)\n\n## Why so closed?\n\nThe threat model is a privacy/off-grid messaging tool whose users de-Google their devices on purpose. Every dependency, every parser, every transport, and every merged-on-trust line of code is attack surface. A small app that does a few things and changes rarely is one I can keep secure and reason about end to end. A feature-accreting app is not. Closing the feature firehose is a security decision, not an unfriendly one — and forking is always open to you.\n\n## If you fork\n\nGreat — that\'s encouraged. Please keep the AGPL-3.0 terms, change the application ID and signing identity (don\'t ship under this project\'s package name or keys), and make clear to your users that your fork is not this project.'}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'persistence', 'evidence': ['KeystoreSecretVault.seal obtains a key from getOrCreateKey(), calls Cipher.getInstance(TRANSFORM), Cipher.init(ENCRYPT_MODE, key) with no parameter spec, reads cipher.iv, and then calls cipher.doFinal(plaintext).', 'The key passed to Cipher.init is produced in a different method, getOrCreateKey(). That method returns a SecretKey loaded from the AndroidKeyStore (KeyStore.getKey) if the alias exists. Otherwise it creates one with KeyGenerator.getInstance(AES, AndroidKeyStore) and kg.generateKey() in a tiered loop.', "The runtime monitor reported 'not observed' (CIPHER-NOBS-00) for a generator of the key at KeystoreSecretVault.kt:69. This is a missing observation, not a positive contradiction, and the monitor cannot distinguish a key loaded from the Keystore or produced in another method from a defective key.", 'In getOrCreateKey, kg.init(spec) and kg.generateKey() run inside a loop over up to three tiers, with failures swallowed. A single KeyGenerator instance can therefore receive more than one init call before a successful generateKey.', 'The KeyGenerator is initialised with a KeyGenParameterSpec (AlgorithmParameterSpec overload). The key size is set in the spec via setKeySize(256), not through init(int).'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Keep the same alias, the same AES/GCM/NoPadding key parameters and the same tier fallback order. Only where the KeyGenerator instance is created moves. Keys already in the Keystore and sealed blobs (iv_len || iv || ct) stay readable.', 'policy_authorized': False, 'usage_grounded_by': {'path': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/KeystoreSecretVault.kt', 'line': 71, 'statement': 'require(iv.size == IV_LEN) {', 'kind': 'fixed_value', 'basis': 'the value is compared with a value fixed in the source, such as a precomputed digest, which a different derivation never matches', 'reached_through': 'assigned to iv'}}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'description': 'Whether the analyzer accepts the patched getOrCreateKey and clears the Cipher.init key-generator finding in seal when it runs again. The existing-alias KeyStore.getKey path is not a named generatedKey producer and may still be reported. The pipeline does not rerun the dynamic analyzer.', 'kind': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C3', 'C4', 'C9']}], 'publication_blocker_record': {'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'blockers': [{'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'kind': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'description': 'Whether the analyzer accepts the patched getOrCreateKey and clears the Cipher.init key-generator finding in seal when it runs again. The existing-alias KeyStore.getKey path is not a named generatedKey producer and may still be reported. The pipeline does not rerun the dynamic analyzer.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}], 'discharged_blockers': [], 'evidence_gap_promoted': [], 'plan_publication_blockers': ['Reviewer checklist: Gradle build of the androidApp module.', 'Reviewer checklist: androidApp unit test task.', 'Reviewer checklist: compilation of the androidTest sources.', 'Reviewer checklist: source recheck that no KeyGenerator instance receives a second init call in the loop.', 'Analyzer reconfirmation is pending: the existing-alias KeyStore.getKey path is not a named generatedKey producer, so the Cipher.init finding in seal may still be reported after the patch. The reviewer should note this. The pipeline does not rerun the dynamic analyzer.'], 'behavior_review': {'status': 'reviewed', 'review_contract_version': 23, 'regression_count': 0, 'patch_has_no_effect': False}}, 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['KeyGenerator.getInstance now sits inside the try block, so a getInstance failure is swallowed and moves to the next tier; if it fails for every tier, the final KeystoreUnavailableException is thrown with lastError as cause. Previously it propagated directly. getInstance for AES on AndroidKeyStore is not expected to fail where tier attempts would succeed.', 'Android Keystore behavior across vendor firmware was not verified on-device.', 'No test was added: the plan lists no required tests and Keystore needs an instrumented environment.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': [], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {'version': 1, 'status': 'not_modelled', 'entries': [], 'required_paths': [], 'limitations': [], 'unresolved_sinks': [], 'unresolved_readers': [], 'unmodelled_sinks': [{'path': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/SecretsRepository.kt', 'line': 75, 'statement': 'prefs.putSealed(key, Base64.encodeToString(vault.seal(value), Base64.NO_WRAP))', 'readers': []}, {'path': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/DatabaseKey.kt', 'line': 59, 'statement': 'prefs.putSealed(PREF_KEY, Base64.encodeToString(vault.seal(fresh), Base64.NO_WRAP))', 'readers': [{'path': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/DatabaseKey.kt', 'line': 41, 'names': 'PREF_KEY', 'statement': 'val existing = prefs.getSealed(PREF_KEY)'}]}], 'source_hashes': {}, 'bound': 'Lexical preference accessors with unique declarations; unresolved identities and index limits are explicit. Other persistence sinks are listed with the statements naming the same constant or literal, unmodelled.'}, 'fix_scope': 'review_only', 'applied_for_validation': True, 'review_contract_version': 23, 'pr_attribution': {'reported_finding': {'csv_class': 'io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.android.storage.KeystoreSecretVault', 'method_name': 'seal', 'spec': 'CipherSpec', 'error_message': 'no generator of the key given to Cipher.init was observed', 'unique_error_id': 'io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.android.storage.KeystoreSecretVault:::seal:::CipherSpec:::UnsatisfiedConstraint:::no generator of the key given to Cipher.init was observed', 'reason': 'seal is untouched. It still gets its key from getOrCreateKey and calls Cipher.init(ENCRYPT_MODE, key) exactly as before. On the existing-alias path the key still comes from KeyStore.getKey, so the checker sees the same call with the same key there.'}, 'attributed_to': [{'csv_class': 'io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.android.storage.KeystoreSecretVault', 'method_name': 'getOrCreateKey', 'spec': 'KeyGeneratorSpec', 'error_message': 'the observed call sequence is not one KeyGeneratorSpec accepts', 'unique_error_id': 'io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.android.storage.KeystoreSecretVault:::getOrCreateKey:::KeyGeneratorSpec:::InvalidSequenceOfMethodCalls:::the observed call sequence is not one KeyGeneratorSpec accepts'}]}, 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '        getKeyOrNull()?.let { return it }\n        val kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES, KEYSTORE_PROVIDER)\n\n        val tiers', 'corrected_method_body': '        getKeyOrNull()?.let { return it }\n\n        val tiers', 'finding_id': '7d98a07e751d', 'branch': 'fix/getorcreatekey-keygeneratorspec-7d98a07e751d-18b2aa8873', 'base_branch': 'main', 'base_commit': 'd731bfdb8a6e13eaabfccf334672a85da1a62d19', 'solution_revision': '18b2aa8873', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_7d98a07e751d_r1/worktrees/io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.native.debug_1.apk/7d98a07e751d/18b2aa8873', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_7d98a07e751d_r1/clones/io.github.thatsfguy.meshcore.native.debug_1.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/KeystoreSecretVault.kt', 'symbol': 'KeystoreSecretVault.getOrCreateKey', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '        getKeyOrNull()?.let { return it }\n        val kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES, KEYSTORE_PROVIDER)\n\n        val tiers', 'corrected_code': '        getKeyOrNull()?.let { return it }\n\n        val tiers', 'reason': 'Remove the single shared KeyGenerator so a fresh instance can be created for each tier attempt.'}, {'source_file': 'androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/KeystoreSecretVault.kt', 'symbol': 'KeystoreSecretVault.getOrCreateKey', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '            try {\n                kg.init(spec)\n                val key = kg.generateKey()', 'corrected_code': '            try {\n                // Fresh KeyGenerator per tier: one getInstance, one init, one\n                // generateKey per instance, so a failed init is never re-inited.\n                val kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES, KEYSTORE_PROVIDER)\n                kg.init(spec)\n                val key = kg.generateKey()', 'reason': 'Obtain a new KeyGenerator inside each tier attempt, so each instance sees exactly one init followed by generateKey.'}], 'changed_files': ['androidApp/src/main/kotlin/io/github/thatsfguy/meshcore/android/storage/KeystoreSecretVault.kt'], 'quality_score': 75, 'explanation': "<!-- pr-title: Create a new KeyGenerator for each key-generation attempt -->\nIn `KeystoreSecretVault.getOrCreateKey`, the code created one `KeyGenerator` for AES and reused it across the tier fallback loop. When a tier's `init` failed, the same instance was initialised again with the next spec before `generateKey`.\n\nRVSec reported that the call sequence on this `KeyGenerator` is not one it accepts. The sequence it expects is `getInstance`, then `init`, then `generateKey`, once per instance. I moved `KeyGenerator.getInstance` inside the `try` in each tier attempt, so every instance gets exactly one `init` and one `generateKey`, and a failed `init` is never retried on the same object.\n\nThe alias, the AES/GCM/NoPadding key parameters and the tier fallback order are unchanged. Keys already in the Keystore and existing sealed blobs stay readable.", 'applied_timestamp': '2026-11-16T05:48:11.701665+00:00'}], 'errors': []}

